g.** Y/y growth went from +3.1% in Q4 2025 to +1.8% in Q1 2026 to –4% in Q2 2026. The Caldrian Electrical Association (CEA) calls Q2 the first decline in three years (n3.d2, n3.d4).\n- **Shipments trail orders by about two quarters.** The Q2 decline therefore reflects weak orders from late 2025 to early 2026. It points to soft shipments through at least H2 2026, and probably into early 2027.\n- **Voltaris revenue is already dropping.** Quarterly revenue was C$905M, C$960M, C$980M and C$890M from Q3 2025 to Q2 2026 (n3.d3). Q2 fell about 9% from Q1.\n- **The last four quarters total C$3,735M.** Reaching C$4.2B would need about 12.4% growth over that. That compares with an industry that is shrinking.\n\n**Implication for 2027**\n- **Flat share:** if Voltaris holds its share and the industry is flat to slightly down in 2027, revenue lands around C$3.6–3.9B. That is about 7–14% below guidance.\n- **Needed to hit guidance:** Voltaris would have to gain share, raise prices, or sell a richer product mix, and the industry data gives no evidence of any of these. Hitting C$4.2B also needs an industry recovery in orders by about H2 2026 or early 2027, and nothing in the data shows one.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The series are short. I have only four quarters of Voltaris revenue and three of industry growth.\n- Q2 may include seasonal or one-off effects.\n- Voltaris's own order book or backlog could offset the industry weakness. I did not look at it. That is the other node's judgment, n2.","ttft_ms":4344,"type":"result","duration_ms":29516,"uuid":"52cc1fef-dba3-4598-b42d-d0dc7386f95a","ttft_stream_ms":3946,"time_to_request_ms":76,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query